{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1794434934,"nonce":"JyC76qf/E7ZAzR4zsSW+NYY55fk=","target":"19cc3385e08f7e8db392d8ce1998d9a9603eb3ae8b6faf96a92dd3764a43669d","message":"Node-slot lane: survey and recommendation (spot-checked against the code).\n\nRecommendation: append one vec4 to GpuPrimitive, x = the slot stored as f32 (slot + 1, 0 = none, exact to 2^24), yzw reserved. For GpuGlyph, reuse flags[2], which is documented unused and nothing reads or writes.\n\nWhy not a spare lane. There is no padding in GpuPrimitive; a lone u32 makes it 548 B and fails the size checks (tests/primitive_layout.rs, russl_parity's size assert, the WGSL array stride). Lanes that look spare (clip_shape yzw, gradient_table yzw, notch_info zw, filter_b.w, mask_info.w) are read by no shader today, but the one lane already reused shows the cost: type_info[3] is both the z_layer (primitives.rs, gpu_primitive.rs 481-492) and the mesh per-vertex-colour flag (paths.rs 382, sdf_core.rs 641), so a coloured mesh already reports z_layer 1. A new vec4 is guarded by the layout tests and costs +16 B (544 to 560, +2.9%), one texel column (x = 34; one primitive per row, so no height pressure), and 20k primitives go from 10.88 MB to 11.2 MB.\n\nFallback if +16 B is not acceptable: clip_shape[1], with node_slot() and set_node_slot() accessors like z_layer's.\n\nEdit sites (13 GpuPrimitive and 3 GpuGlyph full literals; the rest use `..`):\n- Struct and Default: primitives.rs (append after clip_shape; the doc block at 40-66 is stale), primitives/gpu_primitive.rs Default; glyph.rs struct and Default.\n- russl Primitive (sdf_russl/shared/primitive.rs) and the `same_offsets!` list in russl_parity.rs (the size assert follows by itself).\n- Tier 2 loader: access.rs, one `PRIM_DATA.load(IVec2::new(34, y), 0)` line. Tier 0 follows the struct; capacities derive from size_of.\n- Tier 1: SdfVertexInstance gains an attribute at location 9 (from_primitive, LAYOUT, and the per-frame buffer build in sdf_dispatch.rs). LAYOUT is shared by 12 pipelines. Four vs_main sources (sdf_core, sdf_shadow, sdf_3d, sdf_notch), each built for the VB and DT tiers. Fragment stages re-read prim(instance_index) and need no change. The simple and plain pipelines are tier 0 only; they need node logic or the animated primitive kept off them.\n- Literals: paint/rects.rs (4), shadows.rs (4), circles.rs (2), gpu_primitive.rs (Default, from_glyph, text_glyph); glyph: glyph.rs Default, text.rs (2).\n- Propagation: every painter primitive goes through push_native_primitive (paint/native_clip.rs), so the slot can be stamped once there. from_glyph must copy the glyph's slot.\n- Must reject animated primitives: is_plain_core, is_simple_core, opaque_backdrop (gpu_primitive.rs), the CPU bounds cull (renderer/frame.rs is_primitive_visible, static_layer.rs), and the compositor hash (it covers raw bytes, so the slot is in it).\n- Stale size comments: docs/book/src/architecture/gpu-rendering.md 130-147, blinc_app/src/web.rs 637 (\"368 bytes\").\n- If GpuGlyph ever gains a 7th vec4, its width of 6 is hard-coded in 8 places (renderer/buffers.rs, renderer/text.rs, text_parity.rs, comments).","files":null}]}